  "_comment": {
    "about": "Since 1.4.0 this half holds rokctapp's landing page sections (Ray, 2026-09-03: each home SDK holds its own landing page, like profile in Dart): base_sdk >= 1.5.0 carries only the generic landing host (app/landing/page.tsx, components/custom/landing-content.tsx, the page-sections.ts registry, the hero) and this SDK registers its floating nav, chat, logos, social, features, workflow, pricing, comparison, faq and testimonials sections into it, one integrations line each at the // @rokct-sdk-page-sections-start marker, in page order (the installer anchors each line after the previous one). Their copy is components/custom/landing/agent-landing-config.ts. base_sdk composes first. Since 1.5.0 it also holds the hero's chat box (Ray, 2026-09-08: \"chat box is for chat related stuff, i think if agent sdk is home it inject that chat\"): base_sdk 1.7.0's hero carries no input, only a form slot, components/custom/landing/hero-form.ts, a one-marker registry like the others; this SDK installs components/custom/landing/agent-hero-form.tsx - the search-style input, its typewriter placeholders, the submit and the hero-sections.ts results (which that box, not the hero, now loads and renders) - and registers it with one line at // @rokct-sdk-hero-form-start. The form types its props structurally rather than importing hero-form.ts, so against a base_sdk older than 1.7.0 (no hero-form.ts, integration skipped with a warning) the file is installed but unused and the shell still builds with the hero's own box.",
    "components/custom/landing/landing-config.ts": "installed by base_sdk >= 1.5.0 (LandingNavItem for floating-nav.tsx, planSignupUrl for pricing.tsx)",
    "components/custom/landing/page-sections.ts": "installed by base_sdk >= 1.5.0 (the registry the integrations target; PageSectionMeta/PageSectionProps for the section templates)",
    "app/actions/base/landing.ts": "installed by base_sdk >= 1.5.0 (LandingPlan, the plan row type pricing.tsx reads)",
    "lib/actions/getPricingMetadata.ts": "host shell (currency localisation pricing.tsx asks for through agent-landing-config.ts pricing.localize; set it to null to drop it)",
    "components/ui/carousel.tsx": "host shell (chat-section.tsx, social-section.tsx and workflow-section.tsx)",
    "ai/models.ts": "host shell (agent-landing-config.ts reads the paid model id for the {model} token in plan features; the chat surface reads it too)"
  }
}
